# One determinism pin lives under this directory, and it is re-asserted on the cross-platform
# job's live legs — Linux x64 and Android ARM64. (The iOS ARM64 leg is authored and gated off with
# iOS itself, `16` D34.)
#
#   CombatLogReferenceVectors.json — 05 §7's LogHash byte encoding
#
# ⚠️ This file was NOT covered by a rule until M5-12 added it: it inherited the repository root's
# `* text=auto`, which normalises to LF in the index but hands the working tree whatever the
# platform prefers. That was harmless while nothing off-host read it. Pinning eol=lf makes it
# byte-identical on every leg, and makes a one-row addition diff as one row rather than as a
# whole-file rewrite because someone's core.autocrlf disagreed. Same rule as Rng/,
# Model/Snapshots/, Rules/Effects/Determinism/ and game-data/.
#
# 14 §8.2's 10 000-triple LogHash corpus also lived here and was pinned by the same rule. It was
# removed as a brittle self-generated table; the eol=lf rule stays for the vectors above.
*.json text eol=lf
